1
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:02,480
Section thirteen.

2
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:04,810
Harness engineering.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,840
Its purpose is to make a model request measurable

4
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,140
and bounded before it leaves the application.

5
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:16,570
A successful connection alone tells us nothing about decision

6
00:00:16,570 --> 00:00:17,030
quality,

7
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:19,830
safe state changes, or total cost.

8
00:00:28,777 --> 00:00:33,257
The provider inspects the serialized LangChain request, including

9
00:00:33,257 --> 00:00:33,937
destination,

10
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:34,937
model,

11
00:00:35,997 --> 00:00:36,117
instructions,

12
00:00:36,777 --> 00:00:36,897
schema,

13
00:00:37,577 --> 00:00:40,597
output limits, and disabled tool or conversation fields.

14
00:00:41,757 --> 00:00:46,037
The HTTP hook checks current session and workspace authorization.

15
00:00:47,417 --> 00:00:49,457
Counting consumes an HTTP attempt.

16
00:00:50,577 --> 00:00:54,217
Only a successful bounded count permits a monetary reservation

17
00:00:54,217 --> 00:00:55,177
and generation.

18
00:00:55,177 --> 00:00:59,757
SDK retries are disabled to prevent hidden request

19
00:00:59,757 --> 00:01:00,837
multiplication.

20
00:01:06,397 --> 00:01:08,777
Known valid usage settles the estimate.

21
00:01:10,179 --> 00:01:13,619
Refusal or incomplete output is not a successful replay

22
00:01:13,619 --> 00:01:15,719
entry, but can still cost tokens.

23
00:01:17,282 --> 00:01:17,902
Missing usage,

24
00:01:18,522 --> 00:01:21,902
timeout, and uncertain failures keep the maximum reservation.

25
00:01:23,344 --> 00:01:25,824
A bound violation stops later paid admission.

26
00:01:27,207 --> 00:01:30,647
Selected provider rejections have a specific local accounting

27
00:01:30,647 --> 00:01:31,227
policy;

28
00:01:32,267 --> 00:01:35,107
none of these estimates is independent invoice reconciliation.

29
00:01:41,127 --> 00:01:44,187
Fixed mode has audited request and generation limits.

30
00:01:45,517 --> 00:01:49,017
Selective renewal or override preserves past attempts and

31
00:01:49,017 --> 00:01:49,137
spending.

32
00:01:50,447 --> 00:01:53,627
Adaptive mode admits a finite reviewed dollar grant under

33
00:01:53,627 --> 00:01:55,087
the same cumulative cap.

34
00:01:56,278 --> 00:01:59,818
Per-call reservations transfer from a run hold without double

35
00:01:59,818 --> 00:02:00,228
counting.

36
00:02:00,228 --> 00:02:03,128
Recovery links holds to jobs,

37
00:02:04,028 --> 00:02:07,508
releases unused terminal money, and preserves unknown-call holds.

38
00:02:08,999 --> 00:02:11,959
Separate local databases still require reconciliation.
